\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Dear Nadia
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \'a0
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 I am sorry you remain so unwell. 
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \'a0
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 The current position is that my firm is owed around \'a312,000. I remind you that under the terms of the letter of instruction dated 24 January 2024 (attached), you agreed to liquidate your 401K and pay USD30,000 to my firm\'92s client account and provide a bank guarantee. You did not comply with those terms. If you had complied with the terms, I would have sufficient money both to discharge the outstanding fees and continue to act until the liquid sums had been used.
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \'a0
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 If we are reinstructed, then the fees will depend on what we are instructed to do. If it is simply to appear in court for the judgment then Brent will charge a refresher which I anticipate will be \'a38,000. My fees will be incurred on an hourly basis. Brent will then proceed to draft the court\'92s order but that will be a simple process of translating the judgment of the court into the court\'92s order.\'a0 It will not be a case of trying to renegotiate or relitigate what the Judge has decided. 
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \'a0
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 If I am reinstructed, and you ask me to instruct Brent then he will not charge you for carriage of the order (i.e. drafting it in liaison with the other side). That would be included within the brief fee. Obviously, if he has to go to court then he will charge for that (alongside any other consultations that you require). The difficulty for him, I envisage, is that because he does not act on a direct access basis, he would need to be instructed by me which would require you to instruct me. He could not just otherwise draft the order because he would be without instructions from you. I say this because I want to make clear that neither he nor I are attempting to charge you for something (i.e. the drafting of the order) which would otherwise have formed part of the brief fee on the basis of the original instruction. I hope this is clear.
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \'a0
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 To reiterate, the fees which would be incurred to attend a hearing where judgment is handed down to be in the region of \'a35,000 for me and \'a38,000 for Brent. There will also be my fees incurred on an hourly rate for any work I do with Brent and you on the order. This may be 6 hours work at around \'a33k. The total cost will be \'a316,000 on the basis that there is a hearing for the judgment. Less if there is not but at present we do not know how judgment will be handed down.
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \'a0
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 If the judgment is handed down in writing, and there is no hearing then any time will be incurred which does not relate to the simple drafting of the court\'92s order will be charged on an hourly basis by Brent and I. 
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \'a0
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 In any event, in order to resume my firm\'92s instruction the outstanding fees (c.\'a312k) will need to be discharged and I will require a payment on account of \'a316,000.
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \'a0
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 If you have any questions, please let me know.
\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \

\f2\fs26\fsmilli13333 \uc0\u8232 Very best
